<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Songs in History</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Songs of the ancient world</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 23 songs of the ancient world in Songs in History: when and where they were made, what they say and how they sound.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/songs/?e=ancient">Open the songs &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the songs from 1 (the oldest) to 6 (the newest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Guan ju</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Hurrian Hymn No. 6 (Hymn to Nikkal)</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Kesh Temple Hymn</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Gayatri Mantra</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Song of the Sea</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Harper's Songs</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right place next to each song. Their pages will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Song of the Yue Boatman</li><li>Song of Hannah</li><li>Song of the Sea</li><li>Hymn of the Pearl</li><li>Oxyrhynchus hymn</li><li>Phos Hilaron (O Gladsome Light)</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Yangtze River valley, present-day China</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>not known</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>not known (Edessa, if Bardaisan wrote it)</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>not known</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Oxyrhynchus, Egypt</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>ancient Israel (not known exactly)</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Read the words of <b>Kesh Temple Hymn</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Read the words of <b>Hymn to Ninkasi</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one song and listen to its performance. Which instruments or voices do you hear, and how does the music fit the words?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Songs travel: find a song on these pages that was sung far from where it was made, or that gave its tune to another song. How did it travel?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/songs/?e=ancient. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Songs of the ancient world</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Kesh Temple Hymn <span>c. 2600 BCE</span></li><li>Harper's Songs <span>c. 1900 BCE</span></li><li>Hurrian Hymn No. 6 (Hymn to Nikkal) <span>c. 1400 BCE</span></li><li>Gayatri Mantra <span>c. 1200 BCE</span></li><li>Song of the Sea <span>c. 1000 BCE</span></li><li>Guan ju <span>c. 650 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Song of the Yue Boatman <span>1: Yangtze River valley, present-day China</span></li><li>Song of Hannah <span>2: not known</span></li><li>Song of the Sea <span>6: ancient Israel (not known exactly)</span></li><li>Hymn of the Pearl <span>3: not known (Edessa, if Bardaisan wrote it)</span></li><li>Oxyrhynchus hymn <span>5: Oxyrhynchus, Egypt</span></li><li>Phos Hilaron (O Gladsome Light) <span>4: not known</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers quote the song pages.</p></section></div></details>
